  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "items": [
    "The checker replays the authoritative log with separate code",
    "It recomputes to a stated checkpoint, never to whatever is newest",
    "No shared functions with the derivation under audit"
   ],
   "title": "Independent replay"
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "items": [
    "Live state is read at the same checkpoint before comparing",
    "A behind-but-consistent view is lag, proved by catching up",
    "A same-checkpoint difference is corruption, never lag"
   ],
   "title": "Same checkpoint"
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "items": [
    "Detection only pages; repair stays gated behind a human",
    "An incomplete input log bounds what the checker can prove",
    "A bug shared by both code paths stays invisible: say so"
   ],
   "title": "Honest limits"
  }
